# Force binary handling for real test-fixture files. Without this, git's
# own text/binary heuristic (samples the first ~8000 bytes for a NUL byte)
# misclassifies some of them as text — verified live: pdf_blank_page.pdf
# (a genuinely empty PDF page, no embedded font/image data, so no NUL byte
# anywhere near the start) triggered "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on `git
# add`, which would silently corrupt the binary on any checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true (the common default on Windows) — a real, not
# hypothetical, way to break a camelot-parsed PDF fixture after a fresh
# clone. `-text` disables line-ending conversion and diffing outright.
*.pdf -text
*.xlsx -text
*.xls -text
*.ods -text
